{
 "_rule": "THE RE-DERIVATION RULE (xB010, owner instruction 2026-09-17). Sweep first; when the sweep FINDS something the planned work touches or leans on, RE-DERIVE it independently before accepting it, priority on banked NEGATIVES that would stop the work; then DECLARE what you re-derived and what came back, in arc_verdict.json's `rederived` field.",
 "_why": "B1202 and the absence-sweep rule both govern ABSENCE -- neither says what to do when the sweep FINDS something, and a hit reads as 'already settled, move on'. A banked result was treated as an ANSWER; it is a HYPOTHESIS. The asymmetry: a wrong POSITIVE gets re-tested downstream because people build on it; A WRONG NEGATIVE IS NEVER RE-TESTED, BECAUSE IT STOPPED EVERYONE. A bad kill is silent and permanent. Evidence, one session: B742 revived 2 of 33 re-adjudicated kills; xB005's Q3 was a wrong kill caught only because the owner said reverify; B146's justification was wrong though its kill survived; and the seat's one unverified acceptance ('the verification package FAILS') was itself wrong -- its own missing dependencies.",
 "_cite_is_not_rederive": "CITE = read an arc's conclusion and use it. RE-DERIVE = compute the discriminating fact again, in your own sandbox, with your own code where feasible, and compare. Extends E4 (compute the discriminating fact) and E3 (the stale-checkout false negative).",
 "_scope": "'Redo everything' cannot mean all 1248 arcs. The executable form, narrowed in xB010's SEAL rather than silently: REDO EVERYTHING THE PLANNED WORK TOUCHES OR LEANS ON, AND DECLARE ANYTHING YOU DID NOT REDO AND WHY. An honest NOT_RERUN with a reason PASSES the gate -- a rule that forbids saying 'I did not re-run this' does not produce re-derivation, it produces false declarations (the B1222 shape, turned on ourselves).",
 "_mechanism": "A frozen roster, not a numeric cutoff: seat-prefixed ids parse small (xB009 -> 9) so a cutoff could never bind this seat's own arcs. Every arc below existed when the rule landed and is exempt; ANY ARC NOT IN THIS ROSTER MUST DECLARE `rederived`.",
 "_frozen_on": "2026-09-17",
